message:
I see a potential issue in the chunked handling. In the loop:
```c
for (idx = 0; idx < lexer->inbuflen; idx++) {
    if (!isxdigit(lexer->inbuffer[idx])) {
        break;
    }
    chunk_size = strtol((char *)lexer->inbuffer, NULL, 16);
}
```

After this loop, `idx` could be equal to `lexer->inbuflen` if all characters are hex digits. Then:
```c
if (';' != lexer->inbuffer[idx] &&
    '\r' != lexer->inbuffer[idx]) {
```
This reads `lexer->inbuffer[idx]` where `idx == lexer->inbuflen`. Since `inbuflen` max is 9216 and the buffer is 18433, this reads within the array but past the data. Not a stack overflow.

But wait - the `chunked` flag. Let me check if `lexer->chunked` is set in the fuzzer. Looking at the fuzzer code:
```c
lexer_init(&lexer);
lexer.errout.debug = 0;
memcpy(lexer.inbufptr = lexer.inbuffer, Data, Size);
lexer.inbuflen = Size;
```

`lexer_init` is called. Let me check if `chunked` is set there:

<｜｜DSML｜｜>
<parameter=command>grep -n "chunked" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/gpsd/gpsd/packet.c | head -20 && echo "---" && grep -n "lexer_init" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/gpsd/gpsd/packet.c</｜｜DSML｜｜>

